# XAU Dynamics · TickForge — build context exclusions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two jobs: keep the build context small (faster uploads, better cache hits)
# and make it impossible to bake a credential or a local artefact into a
# published layer. Deny-by-default would be safer still, but an explicit list
# stays readable — every secret-bearing pattern below is deliberate.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets and local configuration (never in an image) -------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.crt
*.cer
secrets/
.azure/
.aws/
.kube/
*credentials*
*secret*

# --- Version control and CI ------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.gitlab-ci.yml

# --- Python build and cache artefacts --------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.tox/
.nox/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- Editor and OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Documentation, infrastructure, and tests ------------------------------
# Excluded because the runtime image does not read them; they belong in the
# repository, not in a 24/7 ingestion container.
*.md
!README.md
docs/
infra/
bicep/
*.bicep
*.bicepparam
tests/
notebooks/
*.ipynb
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.log
*.ndjson
*.csv
*.parquet
data/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
Makefile
